# The overview's worked example: state living on a wire.
#
# `total` sends its result back into its own second port, so the
# running sum travels round the loop and is waiting there when the
# next value arrives. Nothing is stored in any box.
#
# The loop needs one value to start with. Deliver a zero to total.1
# before the first input, or the station never has both ports full and
# nothing ever runs.
#
# Fed 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, `seen` collects every running total: 1, 3, 6, 10,
# 15. The order they come back out in is not promised.

station feed keep p entry
  out 0 - total.0

station total add p
  out 0 - total.1
  out 0 - seen.0

station seen keep p result
